# The stand is operated through n100root.sh, which pipes a script over ssh and
# runs it with `sudo -S`. That works only if wheel is allowed to sudo at all.
#
# On the physical N100 it was, and nobody wrote down where from. The VM built to
# replace it was not, so on 15 August 2026 n100root.sh answered "operator is
# not in the sudoers file" for every privileged check on the new stand -- while
# n100.sh, which needs no privilege, worked. A stand that cannot be inspected as
# root is a stand whose service status lies: security.bsd.see_other_uids hides
# other users' processes from an unprivileged caller.
#
# A password is required on purpose. NOPASSWD here would give every wheel member
# unattended root on the build host; the one automated caller that needs it,
# ci_deployer, has its own drop-in beside this file and is limited to a single
# command.
%wheel ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL
